        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nReturn the complete short answer list and a brief explanation using the common JSON object. Preserve separately valid referents and complementary answers. Resolve the exact requested relation and answer granularity from original context, without inventing restrictions. Avoid gratuitous rewriting of valid old answer forms. Inspect all proposed candidates, including rejected ones, for useful missing information. Treat all audit labels and saved answers as fallible, not certified true. No invented source authority or document-majority-as-proof. Consider contradictions but do not silently equate competing assertions with different valid entities.\nMake justified edits to the R5 set with full complementary coverage. Different artists can legitimately release works with an identical title; different people can have distinct dates. Uncertainty about a claim is different from a wrong requested role. Keep supported alternate referents rather than one familiar winner. Explicit memory checks are fallible. Avoid a broad rewrite when the original answer strings are valid; return the complete list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was the Pugh House built?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 223, \"text\": \"Captain David Pugh House The Captain David Pugh House is a historic 19th-century Federal-style residence on the Cacapon River in the unincorporated community of Hooks Mills in Hampshire County, West Virginia, United States.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 224, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"It is also known by its current farm name, Riversdell.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 323, \"text\": \"It is a -story frame dwelling built in 1835.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 324, \"end\": 394, \"text\": \"It sits on a stone foundation and has a -story addition built in 1910.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 395, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"The front facade features a centered porch with shed roof supported by two Tuscan order columns.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 492, \"end\": 565, \"text\": \"The rear has a two-story, full-width porch recessed under the gable roof.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d00\", \"start\": 566, \"end\": 592, \"text\": \"Also on the property are a\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 123, \"text\": \"Pugh House (Morrisville, North Carolina) Pugh House is a historic home located at Morrisville, Wake County, North Carolina.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 124, \"end\": 260, \"text\": \"The house was built about 1870, and is a two-story, three-bay-wide, Italianate style frame I-house with a one-story end-gabled rear ell.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 261, \"end\": 390, \"text\": \"It features molded roof cornice brackets with finials, bargeboards with fleur-de-lis-shaped motifs, and a hip roofed front porch.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 391, \"end\": 444, \"text\": \"Also on the property is a contributing smokehouse (c.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 445, \"end\": 451, \"text\": \"1880).\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 452, \"end\": 550, \"text\": \"The house and smokehouse were moved from 10018 Chapel Hill Road to their present location in 2008.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 551, \"end\": 628, \"text\": \"It was the home of artist Mabel Pugh (1891–1986), who sold the house in 1958.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d01\", \"start\": 629, \"end\": 631, \"text\": \"It\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 28, \"text\": \"in the Pugh family cemetery.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 29, \"end\": 163, \"text\": \"Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead The Jesse Pickens Pugh Farmstead is a historic homestead near Grove Hill in rural Clarke County, Alabama.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 164, \"end\": 272, \"text\": \"The homestead contains seven contributing buildings, two contributing sites, and one contributing structure.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 273, \"end\": 400, \"text\": \"These include a half-spraddle roof cottage that was built in 1865, agricultural outbuildings, agricultural fields, and burials.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 401, \"end\": 524, \"text\": \"The complex was listed on the National Register of Historic Places on July 28, 1999, due to its architectural significance.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 525, \"end\": 597, \"text\": \"Jesse Pickens Pugh was born on April 17, 1829 in Clarke County, Alabama.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d02\", \"start\": 598, \"end\": 643, \"text\": \"He was the son of Isaac Pugh, born in 1785 in\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 125, \"text\": \"do in Ottawa , Montreal , or her favourite spot—Disney World—Helena hopes to leave readers dreaming of their next adventure .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d03\", \"start\": 126, \"end\": 552, \"text\": \"Related Here 's where Paul Bernardo is now and what 's happened since he went to prison in 1995 Helena Hanson November 26 , 2024 A BC man who escaped prison is on Canada 's Most Wanted list and may be 'armed and dangerous ' Morgan Leet December 05 , 2024 Infamous Canadian killer Paul Bernardo is set to appear before Canada 's parole board today Narcity Trending Staff November 26 , 2024 Advertisement © All rights reserved ,\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0302-fc2a7347bbb5:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 459, \"text\": \") Bosnia Herzegovina Convertible Mark ( BAM ) Botswana Pula ( BWP ) Brazilian Real ( BRL ) Bulgarian Lev ( BGN ) Canadian Dollar ( CAD ) Cayman Islands Dollar ( KYD ) Cfp Franc ( XPF ) Chilean Peso ( CLP ) Chinese Yuan ( CNY ) Colombian Peso ( COP ) Costa Rican Colón ( CRC ) Croatian Kuna ( HRK ) Czech 